[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Perspective owns ephemeral view state in the browser

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[DECISION]
UID: DEC-SDOC-PERSPECTIVE-LOCAL-VIEW-STATE
TITLE: Perspective owns ephemeral view state in the browser
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATUS: accepted
RETIRES_ON: View configurations must be shared, synchronized across devices, migrated across incompatible schemas, or governed outside one browser profile.
STATEMENT: >>>
The Perspective view persists only Perspective's native save and restore
tokens, one per named table, in browser localStorage. The server stores no
viewer configuration, and exported canon data is never part of a saved token.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Perspective already serializes its complete view configuration without the
data. Using that contract preserves a useful reload experience without
inventing an application state model.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Ported 2026-09-01 from the codex spike branch; "one per named table" is the
merge's only extension, following the second table.
<<<
